  w3h: "Home PC, mini PC or Raspberry Pi", w3p: "Any Linux machine that stays on 24/7 (a Raspberry Pi 4/5 with a 64-bit OS works). 2 GB RAM or more, 25 GB disk. No port needed; forwarding 26656 on the router helps.",
  hLoop: "Oracle says “Out of host capacity”? Let Cloud Shell retry for you",
  loopIntro: "Free Oracle machines are often full. This script asks for one every 5 minutes (A1 with 6 GB RAM, then Micro with 1 GB) until it gets one. It runs in Oracle's own Cloud Shell, not on your computer, and it is free.",
  l1: "In the Oracle Console, open <b>Cloud Shell</b> (the <code>&gt;_</code> icon at the top right).",
  l2: "Paste the whole script and press Enter. Lines saying <code>Out of host capacity</code> are normal: leave it running.",
